The '''Iguaçuar–Jatiel high speed rail line''', marketed as '''''Gran Sur''''' ({{Literal translation|Big South}}) is a {{convert|673|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} inaugurated on 12 July 1974. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|360|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}, it connects the cities of [[Iguaçuar]], [[Calatañazor]], [[Axarquía]], [[Daramazán]], [[Calabazas]], [[Pasaña]] and [[Jatiel]] in 2 hours and 30 minutes. In Jatiel the line merges into the ''[[Porciúncula–Jatiel high-speed rail line|Direto]].''

Trains are operated by the national [[Baliscan Railways Group]] under the [[AVB]] service. 

